What is a Security Deposit Refund Request Letter?

A Security Deposit Refund Request Letter is a formal written request sent by a tenant to a landlord or property manager asking for the return of a rental security deposit after moving out of a property.

This letter helps provide your forwarding address, payment instructions, move-out date, and an official record of your request. Sending a written request can help speed up the refund process and protect tenant rights.

A Security Deposit Refund Request Letter usually includes:
• Tenant full name
• Rental property address
• Move-out date
• Amount of security deposit paid
• New mailing or bank refund address
• Request for refund payment
• Contact details
• Signature and date

